    art: 
    arrival: 'Sir Aldric: (His helmet speaks from under his arm.) Sir Aldric. I keep
      the lower halls.

      A cellar room. Some company. And no mirrors. I know
      full well what is missing.'
    story:
    - 'Sir Aldric: I lost my head over a wager. Literally. The other knight never
      paid up.'
    - 'Sir Aldric[sad]: Tobias says a dog scratches at the cellar door. I have been
      guarding a dog. For six hundred years.'
    - 'Sir Aldric[happy]: The dog and I have made our peace. A knight may rest when
      his post is relieved.'
    checkout: 'Sir Aldric[happy]: My spur, keeper. You have earned it, defending
      this house.'
    keepsake: Silver Spur
